            <description><![CDATA[<p class="jarvis-headline">Meeting transcripts spell names right.</p>
<h2>Jarvis 0.20.27</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Transcripts now spell the names of the people in your meeting, your contacts and your products correctly, using a small extra model on this Mac. Add your own in Settings → Meetings → "Words Jarvis should know".</li>
  <li>Every meeting is now transcribed from the whole recording after the call, which is more accurate than the live preview.</li>
  <li>On a call without headphones, the other side's voice coming out of your speakers is removed from your microphone before it is transcribed, so their words no longer show up as yours.</li>
  <li>Speaker names from the Google Meet extension now attach to each voice more reliably, including short replies and quick turn-taking.</li>
  <li>Stray "&lt;unk&gt;" marks no longer appear in transcripts.</li>
</ul>
<p>Everything still happens on your Mac. Audio never leaves it.</p>
]]></description>
